		{
			dependencies: ["071A387593153E20"]
			description: [
				"The rod recipe in Lathes use the hard mode (1 rod 2 small dust) recipe, a la GTNH. Most \"harder\" recipe configs are enabled in general (this is subject to change)."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&aVanilla ore gen is still present&r, on top of &1GT ore gen&r. This is to augment the early game, as plain GT making caving irrelevant is antithetical to survival Minecraft in my opinion."
				"Bedrock ore veins are enabled &8but are as of yet unused &r and will be the main method of resource generation. Probably."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Weather (rain, fire, etc.) do &4NOT&r cause machines to explode"
				"On top of this, machine explosions do &4NOT&r cause terrain damage, only delete the machine itself."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Pollution and hazards are enabled. &cPLEASE read the design doc or talk to me directly if you dont vibe with this (or the food changes)"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:iron_gear"
			id: "319A097480599D7F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "20D52FD826E6A266"
				title: "Config Changes"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["071A387593153E20"]
			description: [
				"EMI has its place in any GTM pack, this one is no different."
				"&bAutocrafting has seen an improvement through the EMI Tree Tabs addon.&r This addon allows you to sort different crafting trees into groups and craft those entire groups as if they were one tree. "
				""
				"For example, if you want to craft all the blocks needed for an &aElectric Blast Furnace&r, you can favorite the required recipes, add the individual blocks as recipe trees, and then you can group them together and adjust the number of crafts per item. &cThe addon GUI explains the keybinds&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This replaces the usecase of the old &9Just Enough Calculation&r mod, which allowed you to encode arbitrary recipes (similar to the paper trick in AE2 patterns), which you could exploit to add recipes that gave you the directions for multiblocks and entire processing chains."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:crafting_table"
			id: "7E43A544DD6383E4"
			subtitle: "Emi Memi Imi"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4A3C146F53B99060"
				title: "EMI"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "EMI"
			x: -1.5d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["071A387593153E20"]
			description: [
				"This pack features two mods, Spice of Life &cClassic Edition&r and &6Carrot Edition.&r"
				"&6Carrot Edition&r adds obtaining extra hearts for eating multiple unique types of foods, and&c Classic Edition&r adds diminishing returns on foods that are eaten often. As such, a varied diet is important. Consider finding some animals to farm and crops to breed them with and/or consume yourself. "
				"Both mods have a few items that can aid you on your journey."
				""
				"Also, &lhunger behaves the way it does on Normal difficulty regardless of the one you chose.&r This means that, even on Peaceful, your hunger will fall if you do not eat and you will eventually begin to starve, bringing you down to half a heart."
			]
			icon: "pamhc2foodextended:pepperonipizzaitem"
			id: "2EA70DD3DC788D0B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3E1C70D121EF307B"
				title: "Food"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 1.5d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["071A387593153E20"]
			description: [
				"This pack features the Music Control Reforged mod and C4Music resource pack. These two combine to give you unparalleled control in regards to your ingame music choice. C4Music adds all of the missing music from Volumes Alpha and Beta (and some extras!), while Music Control Reforged adds volume and track control, and also keeps all of the modern music intact with the music category selection, selected with Page Up/Down by default. Volume can also be changed on the fly with the Up and Down arrow keys"
				""
				"By default (i hope) the music selection is on All, the category can be changed with Page Up and Down. All plays all of the music present in the pack, new and old, and removes the context requirements for vanilla music. Everything plays everywhere!"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"You can also select specific music to play by bringing up the music menu (Shift + M by default), or further customize your preferred music from there &8(i have no idea how it works)&r"
			]
			icon: "minecraft:jukebox"
			id: "63E1CEBFBF7C9047"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5380430FA5BBFA9F"
				title: "Music"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["071A387593153E20"]
			description: [
				"This pack features Just Zoom, a highly customizable Zoom mod. Default keybind is Z, configuration menu is B. Also changes the Spyglass in some ways, but these are disabled by default."
				""
				"The keybind zoom is set up to mimic the old Optifine zoom, but you can change this if you wish."
			]
